---
import ProsePage from '../layouts/ProsePage.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';
const updated = 'August 24, 2026';
---

<ProsePage
  title="Terms of Use"
  kicker="Legal"
  description={`The terms governing use of ${site.name}.`}
  lede={`Last updated ${updated}.`}
>
  <p>
    By accessing {site.name} you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use the
    site.
  </p>

  <h2>Use of the site</h2>
  <p>
    You may read, link to, and share our pages freely. You may not scrape the site at a rate that
    degrades service for others, republish articles in full without permission, or present our
    material as your own.
  </p>

  <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    All articles, headlines, photographs, and page designs on this site are the property of
    {site.name} unless otherwise credited. Short quotations for the purposes of commentary,
    criticism, or news reporting are welcome with attribution and a link.
  </p>

  <h2>Nature of the content</h2>
  <p>
    {site.name} is a demonstration publication. Port Meridian and every person, company, agency, and
    institution named in our reporting are invented for the purpose of building and testing a
    realistic publishing environment. Nothing on this site describes real events, and nothing here
    should be relied on as news, legal advice, medical advice, or financial advice. Our
    <a href={withBase('editorial-policy')}>editorial policy</a> explains this in more detail.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party links</h2>
  <p>
    Pages may link to external sites we do not control. We are not responsible for their content,
    accuracy, or privacy practices.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    Advertisements and sponsored placements are labelled. Transactions between you and an advertiser
    are solely between you and that advertiser. See our
    <a href={withBase('advertise')}>advertising page</a> for how we handle commercial content.
  </p>

  <h2>Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
  <p>
    The site is provided “as is,” without warranties of any kind. We do not guarantee that it will be
    available uninterrupted or free of errors.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the fullest extent permitted by law, {site.name} is not liable for any indirect or
    consequential loss arising from your use of the site.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may revise these terms. Material changes will be reflected in the date above.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these terms: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
  </p>
</ProsePage>
